# Lesson Design Rules

## Language (ORT Level / Stage 6)
- About 2–4 sentences per story page; include real dialogue between characters
- Sentence length can be longer (roughly 8–16 words); past tense and simple compound sentences OK
- New words: about 8–12 per lesson; preview with picture + audio
- Each vocab word needs one short **example sentence** (ORT-friendly); tap plays word then sentence
- Prefer natural storybook dialogue over isolated word drills
- Tone: friendly adventure; dragons OK if gentle and playful

## Required lesson structure
1. Cover (title, character, Start)
2. Vocabulary preview (picture + word + example sentence; play AI audio)
3. Story pages (illustration + dialogue lines; play full-line AI audio)
4. Comprehension quiz (instant correct/incorrect feedback + praise)
5. Sight-word / key-phrase practice
6. Follow-up notes for tutor/parent (checkboxes + comments; `localStorage`)

## Audio (preferred)
- Pre-generate neural TTS MP3s with role voices (narrator / George / dragons / family)
- **Character voices:** copy from `scripts/voices.json` into each lesson story JSON — see `docs/character-voices.md` and `.cursor/rules/character-voices.mdc`
- Store under `lessons/assets/lesson-XX/audio/`
- 「Read page」plays full page lines in order with line highlight
- Tap a line / dialogue bubble → play that line’s AI audio
- Quiz: narrator reads the question, then A / B / C; options stay disabled until that finishes
- Generate with `scripts/generate_lesson_audio.py --story ... --out ...` when story or quiz text changes (`--quiz-only` to refresh Q&A clips)

## Technical
- Lesson HTML holds cover/notes markup + `window.LESSON` data
- Shared player: `lessons/css/lesson.css` + `lessons/js/lesson-player.js` (do not fork a second copy per lesson)
- Large fonts (story text ≥ 24–28px), big tap targets, high contrast
- UI suitable for a 5-year-old: big buttons, short labels
- Works offline once the current page’s assets are loaded
- Load **one page at a time** (current + preload next). Never put all story PNG/WebP `src`s in the initial HTML
- Player features to keep: swipe / arrow keys, **Go to** page jump, hash (`#story=3`, `#quiz`), **Auto read**

## Visuals
- Picture-book style illustrations, consistent character design across a lesson
- Match George (and family) to private refs in `lessons/assets/refs/george/` — see `CATALOG.md` and `.cursor/rules/character-refs.mdc`
- Store published lesson images in `lessons/assets/lesson-XX/` (never embed the private ref photos)
- Keep original PNG for redraws; **HTML/player must load `.webp` only** (no JPG copies, no PNG at runtime)
- After adding or replacing a PNG: `python scripts/optimize_lesson_images.py --lesson lesson-XX`
- Story/cover WebP width ≈ 1000px; vocab cards ≈ 800px; keep aspect ratio
- Alt text in English, simple
- How-to: `docs/lesson-player.md`
- After edits: browser smoke test before commit — `.cursor/rules/delivery.mdc`

## Index
- Root `index.html` lists all lessons for the tutor with clear links and short descriptions
